# Project Reflection

This vibe-coding project was interesting (and fun!) to execute. I liked how I was able to create code with the help of AI to ensure my script is matching the goals of my project. It allowed me to code a project that may be have been outside my comfort zone and allowed me to learn in the process. I liked how I was able to be creative and create a project that combined my interests with python data analysis and working with unstructured data! Because I had control of the project, I was able to ensure the process was executed the way I wanted, and I understood how to prompt AI in a way to help me. 

At first, it was overwhelming working with unstrcutured data, as working with tubular data was what I'm used to. It allowed me to explore different data structures and how to transform them into a structure that I can analyze. I learned that extracting dominant colours and creating a palette can be good to visually analyze, but I found it fun to create maps that display how similar pallets are and calculating warmth and brightness. I had the oppurtunity to take what I'm currently used to (python data visualization, strcutured data, analysis, using standard csv/excel formatted data) but also combine this with dealing with non-tubular data! I think I was able to have more fun and creativity with it since it was on a topic I enjoy. 

Overall, working with AI felt like doing code but being able to work at a faster pace with a partner that helped immediately when running into obstacles. It was also beneficial when I had an idea as to what analysis can better relate back to my original goal of colour analysis by destination but wanted to interpret it into code. More time was spent on output analysis, interpretation and creating meaningful insights, since attention and focus wasnt spent debugging code. 
